1
00:00:01,669 --> 00:00:05,309
0 Seconds to Destruction!

2
00:00:06,799 --> 00:00:09,380
According to the Center of Astronomy and Space,

3
00:00:09,380 --> 00:00:12,952
a meteor about 100 meters in size is in direct approach towards Earth.

4
00:00:12,952 --> 00:00:16,335
At today's press conference, Mowtown's Mayor, Mr. Jacques

5
00:00:16,335 --> 00:00:20,675
said that no damage is expected as the meteor will burn up in the atmosphere.

6
00:00:20,675 --> 00:00:23,611
Anna, is that why your dad called you?

7
00:00:23,611 --> 00:00:26,786
Yeah... he said it will be a rare sight in the sky,

8
00:00:26,786 --> 00:00:28,699
so we should try not to miss it!

9
00:00:28,699 --> 00:00:30,503
Glad it wasn't anything serious.

10
00:00:30,503 --> 00:00:34,597
I was worried our cover was blown!

11
00:00:34,597 --> 00:00:39,462
This is footage of the meteor captured by the Lunar Reconnaissance Orbiter.

12
00:00:39,462 --> 00:00:40,503
That's...

13
00:00:40,503 --> 00:00:41,679
What's wrong, Blue Cop?

14
00:00:41,679 --> 00:00:42,959
That's not a meteor.

15
00:00:42,959 --> 00:00:45,173
It's an escape pod from planet Machina.

16
00:00:45,173 --> 00:00:46,469
Really?

17
00:00:46,469 --> 00:00:48,343
I think you might be right.

18
00:00:48,343 --> 00:00:50,408
I wonder who's on board?

19
00:00:50,408 --> 00:00:53,408
Hope it's not another troublemaker like you!

20
00:00:53,408 --> 00:00:54,228
What was that?!

21
00:00:54,228 --> 00:00:55,892
Now is not the time to squabble.

22
00:00:55,892 --> 00:00:57,746
If that's not a meteor...

23
00:01:00,502 --> 00:01:05,870
Then that means it's not going to burn up in the atmosphere, and a giant hunk of metal 100 meters wide will crash straight into the Earth.

24
00:01:05,870 --> 00:01:08,263
The entire town will be blown away without a trace!

25
00:01:08,263 --> 00:01:09,569
What?!

26
00:01:09,569 --> 00:01:14,180
But that means, if there's someone inside, can't you get them to stop or change their trajectory before that happens?

27
00:01:14,180 --> 00:01:15,399
According to the news,

28
00:01:15,399 --> 00:01:17,750
it will soon enter the Earth's orbit.

29
00:01:17,750 --> 00:01:18,995
But there's no sign of it slowing down.

30
00:01:18,995 --> 00:01:20,504
Oh no! Is the pod malfunctioning?

31
00:01:20,504 --> 00:01:23,411
Or is the driver asleep at the wheel?

32
00:01:23,411 --> 00:01:25,742
Oh, so you guys sleep too?

33
00:01:25,742 --> 00:01:28,819
These guys even talk in their sleep and snore like crazy!

34
00:01:29,150 --> 00:01:30,682
Look at this.

35
00:01:30,682 --> 00:01:34,996
This is the drop point of the meteor according to an amateur astronomer.

36
00:01:34,996 --> 00:01:37,259
It's in the middle of Mowtown!

37
00:01:37,259 --> 00:01:40,334
The estimated time of impact is 2:51 PM.

38
00:01:40,334 --> 00:01:42,127
We have less than two hours!

39
00:01:42,127 --> 00:01:45,878
I'll ask my dad to issue an evacuation order right away!

40
00:01:45,878 --> 00:01:48,787
But wait, Anna! What are you going to tell your dad?

41
00:01:48,787 --> 00:01:51,706
That it's not a meteor, but a Metal Cardbot spaceship,

42
00:01:51,706 --> 00:01:53,718
and it's about to crash into the Earth!

43
00:01:54,138 --> 00:01:56,888
Even so, revealing all of this would be a problem.

44
00:01:56,888 --> 00:01:59,448
Yeah! Who would even believe you?

45
00:01:59,448 --> 00:02:01,700
They'll just say it's a tall tale and ignore it.

46
00:02:01,914 --> 00:02:05,688
How about we think of a more effective plan?

47
00:02:05,950 --> 00:02:07,200
What do you think we should do, then?

48
00:02:07,200 --> 00:02:10,625
Just sit by and watch everyone in Mowtown disappear without a trace?

49
00:02:12,722 --> 00:02:15,854
There's one thing that comes to my mind.

50
00:02:23,371 --> 00:02:24,699
Do you think he'll believe us?

51
00:02:24,699 --> 00:02:27,829
We don't have time to wonder! Let's hurry!

52
00:02:28,680 --> 00:02:31,372
Anna and Theo have entered city hall, Jun.

53
00:02:31,372 --> 00:02:33,170
Alright, Blue Cop! Come on home!

54
00:02:33,170 --> 00:02:34,179
Roger that.

55
00:02:34,817 --> 00:02:35,889
How's it going?

56
00:02:35,889 --> 00:02:36,877
All done.

57
00:02:39,468 --> 00:02:40,751
It's ready now.

58
00:02:44,300 --> 00:02:47,477
There. We're connected to the satellite. Now we can communicate with the escape pod.

59
00:02:47,477 --> 00:02:49,406
Wow, Uncle Edo! You're the best!

60
00:02:49,406 --> 00:02:51,795
Stop calling me Uncle!

61
00:02:52,485 --> 00:02:54,585
Ahem.

62
00:02:54,585 --> 00:02:59,343
Attention escape pod! Decelerate immediately and prepare for landing!

63
00:02:59,343 --> 00:03:03,342
I repeat! Decelerate immediately and prepare for landing!

64
00:03:03,342 --> 00:03:04,342
An evacuation order?

65
00:03:04,342 --> 00:03:07,889
That's not a meteorite! It's a spaceship from planet Machina-

66
00:03:07,889 --> 00:03:10,990
No, Anna, you can't...

67
00:03:10,990 --> 00:03:12,211
You said you were an amateur astronomer, right?

68
00:03:12,211 --> 00:03:15,497
Could you explain to me what my daughter is trying to say?

69
00:03:20,780 --> 00:03:27,401
My analysis results show that the meteor consists of Hafnium and Zirconium, along with other materials that make up the outer lining of space ships-

70
00:03:27,401 --> 00:03:31,181
so there is concern that it will not burn up in the atmosphere, therefore crashing directly into the Earth!

71
00:03:31,537 --> 00:03:32,889
Is this true?

72
00:03:32,889 --> 00:03:35,661
I heard it from Blue Cop! So it must be true!

73
00:03:35,661 --> 00:03:36,783
Blue Cop?

74
00:03:36,783 --> 00:03:39,591
It's... the name of my friend's horse!

75
00:03:39,591 --> 00:03:41,929
I don't get it. A horse told you?

76
00:03:41,929 --> 00:03:45,620
No no no! It's the name of a kind robot called a Metal Cardbot.

77
00:03:45,620 --> 00:03:47,211
What kind of joke is this?

78
00:03:47,211 --> 00:03:48,185
Daddy!

79
00:03:48,920 --> 00:03:53,405
This meteorite is being observed by the space institutes around the world,

80
00:03:53,405 --> 00:03:57,459
So try not to worry! We don't want to cause widespread panic, right?

81
00:03:59,336 --> 00:04:00,479
Anna!

82
00:04:01,217 --> 00:04:02,806
Have a nice day!

83
00:04:04,509 --> 00:04:07,752
How could he... he didn't even listen to a word I was saying!

84
00:04:07,752 --> 00:04:09,860
Theo here. Mission failed.

85
00:04:09,860 --> 00:04:13,818
We only have an hour left! Take Anna and go find shelter underground.

86
00:04:17,425 --> 00:04:18,896
And the escape pod?

87
00:04:18,896 --> 00:04:20,427
No word from it!

88
00:04:20,427 --> 00:04:23,610
Are we even sure they're receiving our message?

89
00:04:23,610 --> 00:04:25,264
It's a code used by all Metal Cardbots.

90
00:04:25,264 --> 00:04:26,781
If they can't hear it...

91
00:04:26,781 --> 00:04:28,911
Then their communicator might be broken!

92
00:04:28,911 --> 00:04:32,545
In which case the pod will crash, and it will be over for all of us.

93
00:04:32,545 --> 00:04:34,550
This can't be!

94
00:04:34,550 --> 00:04:36,637
Isn't there anything else we can try?

95
00:04:38,215 --> 00:04:40,629
Let's try sending a control protocol.

96
00:04:40,629 --> 00:04:41,281
What's that?

97
00:04:41,281 --> 00:04:44,987
It's a program that allows us to remotely control the escape pod.

98
00:04:50,144 --> 00:04:51,273
We're connected.

99
00:04:52,771 --> 00:04:55,168
I will change its course now.

100
00:04:55,168 --> 00:04:56,441
Yes please!

101
00:05:01,259 --> 00:05:03,495
The meteorite changed its course?

102
00:05:03,495 --> 00:05:08,838
The space center reported that it seems to be accelerating, but the cause could not be confirmed.

103
00:05:08,838 --> 00:05:10,620
Where is it going to fall?

104
00:05:19,879 --> 00:05:22,470
Over there. That's the escape pod.

105
00:05:24,185 --> 00:05:27,401
The drop point will be about 500 km southwest of Mowtown.

106
00:05:27,401 --> 00:05:29,564
That is... above the ocean.

107
00:05:29,564 --> 00:05:30,393
Then...

108
00:05:30,393 --> 00:05:32,298
It's a success, Uncle Edo!

109
00:05:32,298 --> 00:05:34,824
We did it, Jun!

110
00:05:34,824 --> 00:05:38,567
Mayor Jacques held an emergency conference to announce that the meteorite approaching Earth

111
00:05:38,567 --> 00:05:42,536
is falling into the sea about 500km southwest of Mowtown.

112
00:05:42,536 --> 00:05:45,800
Haha, they did it Anna! The meteor changed its course-

113
00:05:45,800 --> 00:05:47,920
Anna?

114
00:05:48,173 --> 00:05:50,930
What? Anna?

115
00:05:50,930 --> 00:05:51,504
Is that...

116
00:05:51,504 --> 00:05:53,362
It's getting closer!

117
00:05:53,362 --> 00:05:55,350
Hang on, I can't hear-

118
00:05:56,290 --> 00:05:58,540
What... is that...?

119
00:06:00,240 --> 00:06:02,220
Did they detach the escape pod?

120
00:06:02,220 --> 00:06:04,879
Detach?

121
00:06:04,879 --> 00:06:08,110
I think they took off a part of the pod to change its course.

122
00:06:08,110 --> 00:06:09,194
What?!

123
00:06:09,721 --> 00:06:11,958
Where is it falling now?

124
00:06:11,958 --> 00:06:14,338
What?! Mowtown's residential area?!

125
00:06:15,161 --> 00:06:17,800
Is anybody home?

126
00:06:18,562 --> 00:06:21,223
Oh! So it was here!

127
00:06:27,454 --> 00:06:29,908
It will land in about 10 more minutes.

128
00:06:29,908 --> 00:06:31,172
Anna...

129
00:06:36,223 --> 00:06:37,990
I need to get out of here!

130
00:06:38,314 --> 00:06:40,670
Please, somebody help me!

131
00:06:41,610 --> 00:06:43,473
Where could Anna be?

132
00:06:43,473 --> 00:06:43,985
Found her!

133
00:06:46,300 --> 00:06:47,000
Anna!

134
00:06:47,533 --> 00:06:49,567
Mega Trucker, please help!

135
00:06:49,567 --> 00:06:50,733
Leave it to me!

136
00:06:56,499 --> 00:06:57,432
Anna!

137
00:06:59,334 --> 00:07:00,333
Jun!

138
00:07:00,569 --> 00:07:01,855
What are you doing here?

139
00:07:02,418 --> 00:07:04,353
I left your birthday present behind.

140
00:07:04,353 --> 00:07:05,670
Birthday present?

141
00:07:05,747 --> 00:07:08,887
This isn't the time to be chatting.

142
00:07:10,720 --> 00:07:12,410
10 minutes to impact.

143
00:07:16,278 --> 00:07:19,540
We have to figure out a way to stop it!

144
00:07:20,276 --> 00:07:24,569
With a few tweaks, I think I can make your shield even stronger.

145
00:07:25,100 --> 00:07:27,975
Really? Then let's do it right now!

146
00:07:27,975 --> 00:07:33,180
It's not that easy. The stronger the shield, the more energy it consumes, you know?

147
00:07:34,627 --> 00:07:35,757
Your shield!

148
00:07:35,757 --> 00:07:37,836
What about my shield?

149
00:07:37,836 --> 00:07:40,692
Now's the time to combine everyone's strength!

150
00:07:41,691 --> 00:07:44,557
This will sync your power generators.

151
00:07:44,557 --> 00:07:47,754
Then, you can use Mega Trucker's shield to create a forcefield.

152
00:07:47,754 --> 00:07:51,939
Great! Now be generous and send me all your energy till there's nothing left!

153
00:07:51,939 --> 00:07:54,334
Do you really think you can handle all of our energy?

154
00:07:54,334 --> 00:07:57,122
I wonder, what if it fails?

155
00:07:57,122 --> 00:08:00,971
You can't think that way! I believe in you guys!

156
00:08:00,971 --> 00:08:04,898
I know you will keep our town safe by working together!

157
00:08:04,898 --> 00:08:07,254
If that's the case, looks like we'll have to give it a shot.

158
00:08:07,254 --> 00:08:09,910
Y-Yes! Let's do our best!

159
00:08:09,910 --> 00:08:11,843
I believe in you too.

160
00:08:11,843 --> 00:08:13,788
Because Jun is my friend.

161
00:08:22,673 --> 00:08:24,435
I believe in you too!

162
00:08:24,435 --> 00:08:25,706
Thank you.

163
00:08:25,706 --> 00:08:28,495
Now let's repay that trust!

164
00:08:29,954 --> 00:08:32,110
Alright. Everyone, get ready!

165
00:08:32,110 --> 00:08:33,234
Got it!

166
00:08:39,225 --> 00:08:40,586
We're ready!

167
00:08:41,177 --> 00:08:42,552
Okay!

168
00:08:42,552 --> 00:08:44,721
Energy full charge!

169
00:09:24,769 --> 00:09:25,868
Blue Cop?!

170
00:09:25,868 --> 00:09:28,687
It's okay, Mega Trucker! I got your back!

171
00:09:29,158 --> 00:09:30,500
I'll help, too!

172
00:09:30,500 --> 00:09:31,244
-Me too!
-And me!

173
00:09:33,822 --> 00:09:35,937
Guys! You got this!

174
00:09:40,408 --> 00:09:43,413
Everyone, give it your all!

175
00:09:48,677 --> 00:09:50,341
Ultra... Mega...

176
00:09:50,341 --> 00:09:52,403
Power Shield!!

177
00:10:15,200 --> 00:10:16,235
You did it...

178
00:10:17,782 --> 00:10:19,447
Are you alright, Mega Trucker?

179
00:10:19,447 --> 00:10:21,884
This is nothing! I'm fine!

180
00:10:22,793 --> 00:10:23,552
Jun.

181
00:10:23,942 --> 00:10:25,211
Anna...

182
00:10:25,211 --> 00:10:29,163
I want you to know, I promise I'll keep the Metal Cardbots a secret.

183
00:10:29,163 --> 00:10:31,754
Thank you, Anna. And...

184
00:10:31,754 --> 00:10:34,408
I'm sorry I lied all this time.

185
00:10:34,408 --> 00:10:38,580
No, no! I'm sure I would have done the same if I were you.

